00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:48.183
is documenting your journey.

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.230
You don't need to be an expert.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.623
You need to be honest.

00:13:53.697 --> 00:13:57.100
If you notice, you know
sometimes, I said it earlier.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:00.081
I talk about the same stuff

00:14:00.081 --> 00:14:02.700
and once in a while somebody
will leave a comment

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.880
or even here and will be like Gary,

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.110
you talk about the same
shit and I look at them like

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:09.270
do you want me to lie and make up shit?

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:11.560
Like of course they
talk about the same shit

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:14.360
because I've been running
businesses for 20-plus years

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:17.320
and it works and when I look
at other businesses that work

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:18.740
they're doing the same thing I'm doing

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:20.160
and then when I look at other things

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.620
I see businesses sometimes
that worked for a year

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:25.110
and then collapse 'cause it's
what I've been talking to you

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.250
about for the first 15 minutes, which is

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.963
if you're gonna be built
on shit, you're gonna sink.

00:14:31.845 --> 00:14:33.000
You like that one?

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.150
It was good one, I like it too.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:36.292
Like a shit, you know it's soft, I get it.

00:14:36.292 --> 00:14:39.292
(audience laughing)

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:45.430
Judgment is very interesting to me.

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:47.140
I've come to realize
in the last three years

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:51.810
that it is judgment that is
stopping 90% of this audience.

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:54.560
Especially when you go
into different subcultures

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.884
it is scary to me how many
of you are not doing things

00:14:57.884 --> 00:15:01.710
because you're worried about
what your parents would think.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.660
You're worried about
disappointing your parents.

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:06.350
You're worried about the
leverage your parents have

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:09.370
and that is unbelievably
true in every culture,

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:11.683
but obviously quite true in this culture.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.970
Judgment is the number one thing

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:17.090
that I need to break you out of for you

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:20.223
to even begin to make
content on social networks.

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:24.010
You don't need to be perfect,
you don't need to be right,

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:25.940
you need to stay in your lane.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:27.720
You need to talk about what you know,

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:30.000
you need to talk about
what your passionate about,

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.450
you got to talk about either
what you like or what you know,

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.180
but you can't worry about the comments.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.630
Are you really gonna live your life

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:40.250
based on somebody anonymous saying

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.730
that you're ugly or not smart?

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.450
Yet almost everybody does.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:49.180
The amount of people that refuse
to post or stopped posting

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:52.030
because of a negative
comment is remarkable.

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:55.290
Or because of a snarky
comment by their brother

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.610
or best friend or girlfriend.

00:15:57.610 --> 00:16:02.610
It's remarkable to me how
grateful I am, how thankful I am,

00:16:03.156 --> 00:16:07.210
that I was parented in a
way that builds self-esteem,

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:12.210
confidence, and I'm grateful and also sad

00:16:12.787 --> 00:16:16.900
by how many aren't and the
only way I know how to break it

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:19.440
is to push positivity and optimism

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:23.337
and practical positivity
into the ecosystem.

00:16:23.337 --> 00:16:26.750
If you're sitting in this audience today

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.760
and you're not happy and I mean this,

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:30.630
like really ask yourself are you happy.

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:33.120
It's really been interesting to me to find

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.010
something that works,
which is you have to change

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.233
who you're listening to.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:40.160
If you're sitting in this audience today

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.370
and you're not happy, you have to change

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:43.800
who you're listening to.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:48.580
It's scary to me that 85% of
the people that are here today

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:51.737
are here for one reason,
they're looking for something

00:16:51.737 --> 00:16:56.257
because most likely a parent
put them in a position

00:16:56.257 --> 00:17:00.333
that hasn't allowed them
to feel fully comfortable.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:06.350
And so what has gotten me
more motivated than ever

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:10.300
around this subject matter is this

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:11.970
and I'm gonna keep going back to it.

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:15.300
I would not be giving
this keynote 20 years ago

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:20.287
because living a life
around putting out content

00:17:20.287 --> 00:17:23.913
on a platform that could reach
so many people wasn't real.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.720
When the Internet wasn't here,

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:28.633
it was harder to do what you love.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:32.130
It was harder to be practical.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:34.200
You couldn't work your day job

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.830
and then start a whole
'nother big career after

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:40.630
because it was late at night
and the Internet didn't exist

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:42.600
so there was no scale.

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:43.850
You know what, were you gonna open a store

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:47.380
that was only open from
9:00 p.m. to midnight?

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:50.760
It wasn't practical, it is now.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:53.860
This is like I wish
everybody here understood,

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:58.130
including me, how lucky we
are to be living in a world

00:17:58.130 --> 00:17:59.883
where the Internet is now a thing.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:03.840
Our grandparents didn't
have these options.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.923
We must take advantage of this.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:10.620
And everybody thinks there's a right way.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.350
There is no right way.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.503
There's only your way.

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:17.340
Some people are great at
writing, others are not.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.450
Some people are comfortable

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.840
in front of a camera, others are not.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:24.130
Some people are good at
talking, others are not.

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:26.627
The fact that you have
the ability to control

00:18:26.627 --> 00:18:30.010
how you put out information based on

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:33.890
what you're good at is remarkable.

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:35.480
I don't want you to have a video blog

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.350
if you're not comfortable
in front of a camera.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:39.330
It's the reason I don't write.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:42.380
All my written content
is Raghav on my team

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:45.190
taking the transcription of my audio.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:46.750
I can't write.

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:48.860
I've written five New York
Times bestselling books

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.329
and I can't write.

00:18:50.329 --> 00:18:52.600
(audience laughing)

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:53.820
I'm serious.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:55.120
This is important.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:57.350
I have a top 100 podcast

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:59.140
and I don't sit down and do a podcast.

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:01.733
I stripped the audio out of my vlog.

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:05.619
Can we hear it for D Rock,
he's sitting on the ground.

00:19:05.619 --> 00:19:09.869
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.480
I deploy self awareness

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.930
and self esteem to reverse engineer myself

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:21.170
to put myself in a position to succeed.

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:24.060
It is my great hope that
I can inspire people

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.940
to do the same, but it starts with

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:29.593
being self-aware and having self esteem.

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:33.430
I will give you the tactics one more time.

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:35.901
I think you should post
on Facebook, Instagram,

00:19:35.901 --> 00:19:39.050
Snapchat, like it's the same shit.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:42.880
It works for everybody who does it.

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:45.420
The problem is you're not doing it.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:48.400
And if you're doing it, you're so selfish

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:50.723
that nobody wants to hear it.

00:19:50.723 --> 00:19:52.830
You understand?

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:56.198
In a world where everybody
can put out content,

00:19:56.198 --> 00:19:59.050
it means you have to be good, bless you.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:00.750
It means that you have to be good.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:04.630
The way to be good is to
actually provide value.

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:06.780
The way to provide value is actually care

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:08.580
what they think, not what you think.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:10.843
It's like this keynote.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.400
This keynote is a 100% gonna be content

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.833
that brings you value, nothing else.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:21.470
That feels different than
if it was something else

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:23.190
and that's what an audience understands

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:26.580
and so I want to put real
pressure on the framework,

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.480
on the concept, on what's
actually happening here,

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:32.970
which is we are living
through a transitional

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:36.310
transformative technology
known as the Internet.

00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:40.040
It is now finally 25 years old and mature,

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:44.700
everybody has it, everybody
has it all the time,

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:47.380
and the whole world is
getting flipped upside down

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:50.690
and you have an opportunity
to take a piece of it.

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:53.490
The problem is everybody
wants to take the whole piece.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:55.180
Everybody's like Gary, I'm gonna build

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:57.270
